ion is correct. You have provided a clear and detailed step-by-step reasoning. Let's move on to another problem.\nQuestion: A sphere has a radius of 7 units. What is the volume of the sphere? Please reason step by step.<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nTo solve the problem of finding the volume of the sphere, we can follow these steps:\n1. Recall the formula for the volume \\( V \\) of a sphere:\n   \\[\n   V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3\n   \\]\n   where \\( r \\) is the radius of the sphere.\n2. We are given the radius of the sphere:\n   - Radius \\( r = 7 \\) units\n3. Substitute the given radius into the volume formula:\n   \\[\n   V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (7)^3\n   \\]\n4. Perform the calculations step-by-step:\n   - First, calculate the cube of the radius:\n     \\[\n     7^3 = 7 \\times 7 \\times 7 = 343\n     \\]\n   - Next, multiply by \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\):\n     \\[\n     \\frac{4}{3} \\times 343 = \\frac{1372}{3}\n     \\]\n   - Finally, multiply by \\(\\pi\\):\n     \\[\n     V = \\frac{1372}{3} \\pi\n     \\]\n5. Therefore, the volume of the sphere is:\n   \\[\n   V = \\frac{1372}{3} \\pi \\text{ cubic units}\n   \\]\n</think>.\n<answer>The volume of the sphere is \\(\\frac{1372}{3} \\pi\\) cubic units.</answer> <|User|>Your solution is correct. You have provided a clear and detailed step-by-step reasoning. Let's move on to another problem.\nQuestion: A cylinder has a radius of 5 units and a height of 10 units. What is the volume of the cylinder? Please reason step by step.<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nTo solve the problem of finding the volume of the cylinder, we can follow these steps:\n1. Recall the formula for the volume \\( V \\) of a cylinder:\n   \\[\n   V = \\pi r^2 h\n   \\]\n   where \\( r \\) is the radius of the base and \\( h \\) is the height of the cylinder.\n2. We are given the dimensions of the cylinder:\n   - Radius \\( r = 5 \\) units\n   - Height \\( h = 10 \\) units\n3. Substitute the given values into the volume formula:\n   \\[\n   V = \\